2026-09-27T04:48:01.5728952Z Description:
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5729316Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5729543Z 
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5730170Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5730832Z 
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5730932Z Update Note
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5731186Z ===========
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5731495Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5731756Z 
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5731860Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5732121Z ================
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5732235Z 
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5732396Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5732931Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5733114Z 
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5733256Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5733553Z ====================================
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5733727Z 
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5733865Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5734194Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5734594Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5735163Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5735522Z 
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5735684Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5736075Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5736504Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5736796Z 
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5737030Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5737350Z 
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5737438Z Packages
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5737700Z ========
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5737801Z 
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5738717Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5739625Z 
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5739848Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5740297Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5740699Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5741187Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5741695Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5742049Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5742873Z 
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5743250Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5743521Z ==========================
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5743672Z 
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5744487Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5745420Z 
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5745921Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5746608Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T04:48:01.5746801Z 
